{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "02602",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 1.32,
      "end_seconds": 4.37,
      "duration_seconds": 3.05,
      "text": "Morning, doctor. Lovely to meet you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 6.19,
      "end_seconds": 10.74,
      "duration_seconds": 4.55,
      "text": "Not at all, please sit. What seems to be wrong?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 12.55,
      "end_seconds": 18.62,
      "duration_seconds": 6.07,
      "text": "I've been passing kidney stones, and I wanted to get it checked."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 19.18,
      "end_seconds": 20.6,
      "duration_seconds": 1.42,
      "text": "Since when exactly?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 22.3,
      "end_seconds": 28.43,
      "duration_seconds": 6.13,
      "text": "Around three weeks... no wait, you know, it's more like four weeks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 29.38,
      "end_seconds": 32.0,
      "duration_seconds": 2.62,
      "text": "How much does it limit you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 33.34,
      "end_seconds": 47.05,
      "duration_seconds": 13.71,
      "text": "Mostly mild. I've also had constipation. And aching bones, too. As for aching bones, it's every other day. Uh, I had being thirsty before. That's settled now, though."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 48.93,
      "end_seconds": 53.86,
      "duration_seconds": 4.93,
      "text": "Have you been passing kidney stones at any time before this?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 55.62,
      "end_seconds": 62.48,
      "duration_seconds": 6.86,
      "text": "I, I had a similar thing about six months ago. It went away."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 64.39,
      "end_seconds": 65.96,
      "duration_seconds": 1.57,
      "text": "How about low mood?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 71.91,
      "end_seconds": 75.42,
      "duration_seconds": 3.51,
      "text": "Not that I've noticed, no low mood."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 76.64,
      "end_seconds": 80.1,
      "duration_seconds": 3.46,
      "text": "And what about weight loss, fractures or fever?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 83.66,
      "end_seconds": 86.09,
      "duration_seconds": 2.43,
      "text": "No, nothing to report there."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 86.68,
      "end_seconds": 89.49,
      "duration_seconds": 2.81,
      "text": "Has your heart given you any trouble?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 91.58,
      "end_seconds": 94.63,
      "duration_seconds": 3.05,
      "text": "Okay, so no, that's been fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 95.88,
      "end_seconds": 98.44,
      "duration_seconds": 2.56,
      "text": "And your skin, any changes there?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 99.66,
      "end_seconds": 103.41,
      "duration_seconds": 3.75,
      "text": "Um, nothing on the skin, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 104.94,
      "end_seconds": 109.33,
      "duration_seconds": 4.39,
      "text": "Can you list what you take, tablets, creams or inhalers?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 110.21,
      "end_seconds": 123.95,
      "duration_seconds": 13.74,
      "text": "I take omeprazole, 20 milligrams, once a day. I do miss it now and then, to be fair. Oh, it's propranolol, 40 milligrams, twice a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 137.08,
      "end_seconds": 140.41,
      "duration_seconds": 3.33,
      "text": "Okay, do you have any chronic illnesses?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 141.73,
      "end_seconds": 146.09,
      "duration_seconds": 4.36,
      "text": "I've got acid reflux. I, I have migraines."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 147.65,
      "end_seconds": 154.51,
      "duration_seconds": 6.86,
      "text": "Are there any allergies I should be aware of? These questions might sound routine, but they matter."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 155.29,
      "end_seconds": 170.54,
      "duration_seconds": 15.25,
      "text": "I was told I'm allergic to kiwi, but I don't remember what reaction I had. I was told I'm allergic to cat fur, but I don't remember what reaction I had."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 171.56,
      "end_seconds": 174.95,
      "duration_seconds": 3.39,
      "text": "What do you do during the day?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 175.66,
      "end_seconds": 179.22,
      "duration_seconds": 3.56,
      "text": "I look after my grandchildren most days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 180.38,
      "end_seconds": 182.66,
      "duration_seconds": 2.28,
      "text": "Do you get out much?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 183.83,
      "end_seconds": 187.64,
      "duration_seconds": 3.81,
      "text": "Not much, I mostly stay in these days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 201.27,
      "end_seconds": 204.13,
      "duration_seconds": 2.86,
      "text": "I'll just record a few vital signs."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 210.59,
      "end_seconds": 213.47,
      "duration_seconds": 2.88,
      "text": "Bear with me while this finishes..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 226.33,
      "end_seconds": 238.79,
      "duration_seconds": 12.46,
      "text": "Okay: heart rate 65, weight 65 kilos, BMI works out to 20.5. And blood pressure 119 over 73, height 178 centimetres, temperature 36.6."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 239.45,
      "end_seconds": 241.12,
      "duration_seconds": 1.67,
      "text": "Is that okay?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 243.02,
      "end_seconds": 245.38,
      "duration_seconds": 2.36,
      "text": "I'll interpret them after the examination."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 248.1,
      "end_seconds": 250.94,
      "duration_seconds": 2.84,
      "text": "Okay, time for me to examine you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 251.8,
      "end_seconds": 252.5,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Right."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 253.48,
      "end_seconds": 254.65,
      "duration_seconds": 1.17,
      "text": "Breathe out slowly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 264.0,
      "end_seconds": 268.8,
      "duration_seconds": 4.8,
      "text": "Your examination is normal and there is no tenderness over the bones."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 271.43,
      "end_seconds": 273.08,
      "duration_seconds": 1.65,
      "text": "Please sit back down."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 283.73,
      "end_seconds": 299.02,
      "duration_seconds": 15.29,
      "text": "Having listened and examined, I think we're dealing with possible raised calcium from an overactive parathyroid at this stage. It could also be vitamin D excess, so we'll keep that open."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 301.12,
      "end_seconds": 303.34,
      "duration_seconds": 2.22,
      "text": "Is it dangerous, doctor?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 305.38,
      "end_seconds": 340.7,
      "duration_seconds": 35.32,
      "text": "It's reasonable to be concerned, but right now possible raised calcium from an overactive parathyroid is my leading thought, not anything worse. Let's get a calcium and parathyroid hormone test, for kidney stones. A kidney ultrasound is what I'd like next, for kidney stones. It's a routine test and it'll give us a much clearer picture. Let's get a bone density scan, for possible hyperparathyroidism. Drink plenty of water and avoid calcium supplements until the results."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 341.93,
      "end_seconds": 356.77,
      "duration_seconds": 14.84,
      "text": "Cut back on tea, coffee and fizzy drinks for a couple of weeks and see how things settle. Let's get you seen by the endocrine clinic, I'll arrange the letter."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 358.49,
      "end_seconds": 362.0,
      "duration_seconds": 3.51,
      "text": "Sure, um, where do I go?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 363.2,
      "end_seconds": 379.5,
      "duration_seconds": 16.3,
      "text": "Keep an eye out, and if the symptoms get worse, call us the same day or go to emergency. I'll want another look after the results. That's everything on my side. Anything you're unsure about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 380.14,
      "end_seconds": 383.67,
      "duration_seconds": 3.53,
      "text": "Right, I'll do that. Thank you, doctor."
    }
  ]
}